From b24debc9c60addab70db6991cc386cda5d2a878a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:01:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09294/11362] Ship the vLLM backend for the scored path: 651.8
 tok/s at k=32, 12.5x

Operator-directed migration (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6510) on the measurement in
okf/claims/vllm-native-fp4-blackwell.md: native SM120 cutlass FP4 plus fp8 KV
plus continuous batching reached 651.8 tok/s aggregate at k=32 on the actual
scored card, against 228.3 for the best llama.cpp configuration and roughly 52
for what shipped. That takes the induction budget from does-not-fit to about
2.6 hours of the 11.5-hour cap.

A SECOND BACKEND, NOT A REPLACEMENT, and that is the whole safety argument. The
dev 3090s are sm_86 and cannot execute NVFP4 at all, so llama.cpp stays the
local and conductor path. The scoping estimate feared rewriting ~60 test files
that pin llama.cpp specifics; none needed changing, because they pin the path
that is still the default. 104 of them pass unchanged, which is the claim
verified rather than asserted.

CARNOT_ARC_LLM_BACKEND=vllm is the only thing that switches backends. Unset,
empty, "llamacpp" and any typo all resolve to llama.cpp -- a malformed env var
must never silently migrate the scored generator to a backend the local cards
cannot run.

WHAT WAS REUSED RATHER THAN REBUILT. The request path was already
OpenAI-compatible, so /v1/chat/completions needed nothing. Only llama.cpp's raw
/completion route required translation, and the reply is reshaped INTO
llama.cpp's response contract -- content, stop_type (length->limit, stop->eos),
timings.predicted_n -- so _record_completion_diagnostics and every truncation
and limit diagnostic downstream keep reading the fields they were written
against. Dropping any one of those would silently disable truncation detection.

The reuse guard is ported in policy, not in mechanism: vLLM serves no /props,
so identity comes from /v1/models, and the rule stays REFUSE-and-relaunch
rather than adopt. Adopting a stale server is how a run induces with the wrong
model while its own witness reports the intended one.

MTP is deliberately not configured here. Batching beat speculation decisively
at concurrency (llama.cpp measured 228.3 batched against 108.8 with MTP on at
k=16) and vLLM's own MTP interaction with batching is unmeasured, so the
instance records why rather than letting a run believe it had speculation.

max_num_seqs defaults to 24 from the memory arithmetic and the measured curve,
not from taste: fp8 KV fits about 22 concurrent sessions at capped production
length in the ~61 GB KV budget, and k=16->32 already gained only 1.35x.

The kernel selects the backend only when a safetensors model directory is
actually attached, resolved by rglob because Kaggle's dataset mount depth is
not stable across runs. It also applies the two environment repairs the
benchmark proved necessary before the agent starts: the coherent CUDA 13.0.x
toolchain, and unversioned linker symlinks with the driver located via ldconfig
rather than guessed.

13 new tests covering the opt-in gate, the response reshape both ways, the
reuse refusals, and the fail-open when /v1/models is unreachable.

